  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Iowa received $80M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 96.2% year over year. Award activity so far includes 282 awards, with an average award size of $284K. Year-to-date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Fiscal-year comparisons show steep swings: FY22 totaled $3B, FY23 totaled $4.3B, FY24 totaled $3.6B, FY25 totaled $4.7B, FY26 totaled $2.1B, and FY27 totaled $80M. The Department of the Treasury was the largest buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $31.2M, followed by the Department of Justice with $13.5M and the Department of Agriculture with $11.3M. PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. was the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $28.2M in obligations. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying is the largest industry by obligation in FY2027 to date with $28.2M. The data show concentrated fiscal-year activity and a much smaller current-year total compared with recent completed fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date totaled $80M in obligations. Prior full fiscal years ranged from $2.1B to $4.7B: FY22 totaled $3B, FY23 totaled $4.3B, FY24 totaled $3.6B, FY25 totaled $4.7B, and FY26 totaled $2.1B. Obligations fell 96.2% year over year. The FY2027 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries account for most FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury led buying with $31.2M, followed by the Department of Justice with $13.5M and the Department of Agriculture with $11.3M. PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. led vendors with $28.2M, followed by ADVANCED TECHNOLOGIES GROUP LLC with $10.9M and THE UNIVERSITY OF IOWA with $4.8M. Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying led industries with $28.2M, followed by Software Publishers with $10.4M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $5.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
