      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Iowa?",
      "a": "Iowa received $80M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 282 awards with an average award size of $284K. Fiscal-year totals for previous years were larger: FY22 totaled $3B, FY23 totaled $4.3B, FY24 totaled $3.6B, FY25 totaled $4.7B, and FY26 totaled $2.1B. Obligations fell 96.2% year over year."
